    "productType": "MULTIDAYTOUR",
    "name": "Cape2Camp End to End 7 Days",
    "shortDescription": "7 Days, 6 Nights, 135 km of Adventure! \r\nExplore the Capes Classic from Cape Naturaliste to Cape Leeuwin with Cape2Camp. We take care of the details—meals, transport, and camp setup—so you can focus on the journey. \"We keep you on Track\"",
    "description": "<h4><br></h4><h4>7 Days, 6 Nights, 135 km of Adventure!&nbsp;</h4><p>Embark on the iconic End-to-End Cape to Cape Track from Cape Naturaliste to Cape Leeuwin with Cape2Camp. This moderate to challenging hike offers breathtaking views and diverse terrains. We handle the details—transport, meals, accommodation—so you can focus on the journey. \"We keep you on track!\" &nbsp;</p><p>✅&nbsp;<strong>No daily transfers needed</strong>&nbsp;– Enjoy a true self-guided experience.<br>✅&nbsp;<strong>Comfortable tented accommodation</strong>&nbsp;– With bedding provided, you’ll sleep soundly under the stars.<br>✅&nbsp;<strong>All meals &amp; drinks included</strong>&nbsp;– Including delicious local wine and beer.<br>✅&nbsp;<strong>Hand-luggage transfers between campsites</strong>&nbsp;– We carry your luggage, so you can focus on your hike.<br>✅&nbsp;<strong>24/7 phone support &amp; WhatsApp group</strong>&nbsp;– Stay connected and get support throughout your journey.<br>✅&nbsp;<strong>Sustainable hiking</strong>&nbsp;– We prioritise&nbsp;low-impact camping and support local produce.</p><p><strong><br></strong></p><p><strong>Day 1: Cape Naturaliste to Yallingup (14 km)</strong><br>Start your adventure at&nbsp;Cape Naturaliste Lighthouse, taking in sweeping ocean views. Hike along the&nbsp;Cape Naturaliste Ridge, offering stunning views of the coast—great for setting the tone for your adventure. Pass&nbsp;Sugarloaf Rock&nbsp;and continue to&nbsp;Yallingup, where you can enjoy a refreshing swim in the&nbsp;Yallingup Lagoon, a real treat after your hike. Relax at&nbsp;Yallingup Beach Caravan Park&nbsp;for the night, and enjoy dinner at&nbsp;Caves House Restaurant&nbsp;(own cost) for a cosy dining experience.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Day 2: Yallingup to Moses Rock (18 km)</strong><br>Begin your hike from&nbsp;Yallingup, passing&nbsp;Smiths Beach&nbsp;and the tranquil&nbsp;Injidup Spa, famous for its natural rock pools that offer the perfect spot for a rejuvenating swim. Continue along coastal paths, arriving at&nbsp;Moses Rock. A transfer back to&nbsp;Yallingup&nbsp;will await, where you’ll stay another night at&nbsp;Yallingup Caravan Park, enjoying the peaceful setting and perhaps relaxing for the evening.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Day 3: Moses Rock to Gracetown (16 km)</strong><br>Hike along&nbsp;Wilyabrup Cliffs, offering breathtaking coastal views. Continue along scenic trails to&nbsp;Gracetown, where you can enjoy a shower before heading to&nbsp;Grace Farm&nbsp;for an optional wine tasting across the road. Stay overnight at&nbsp;Gracetown Caravan Park, nestled inland and offering a serene environment for a restful evening.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Day 4: Gracetown to Prevelly (20 km)</strong><br>Hike through&nbsp;Cowaramup Bay, known for its clear waters, and pass&nbsp;Ellensbrook Homestead. Reach the&nbsp;Margaret River Mouth&nbsp;and enjoy stunning views where the river meets the ocean. In the evening, enjoy dinner at&nbsp;Seagarden Café&nbsp;(own cost), offering beautiful views of&nbsp;Margaret River Mainbreak&nbsp;and a stunning sunset. Stay at&nbsp;Prevelly Caravan Park, with its peaceful beachside setting.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Day 5: Prevelly to Conto (19 km)</strong><br>Hike through&nbsp;Boodjidup Brook&nbsp;and&nbsp;Redgate Beach, known for its striking red rocks. Explore&nbsp;Bob's Hollow&nbsp;before arriving at&nbsp;Contos Cliff, where panoramic ocean views await. Walk into&nbsp;Conto Campground, nestled in the tranquil&nbsp;Boranup Forest, where you may encounter wildlife like kangaroos and emus. Settle in and relax for the night.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Day 6: Conto to Hamelin Bay (22 km)</strong><br>Walk through the&nbsp;Boranup Forest, lined with towering karri trees. Continue along to&nbsp;Boranup Beach, where you can enjoy stunning coastal vistas. Arrive at&nbsp;Hamelin Bay, known for its friendly stingrays. Stay at&nbsp;Hamelin Bay Holiday Park, just steps from the beach, and unwind in this peaceful location.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Day 7: Hamelin Bay to Cape Leeuwin (26 km)</strong><br>Hike along rugged coastal cliffs, passing the dramatic&nbsp;Blowholes at Cosy Corner, where the ocean’s power is on full display. Continue on to&nbsp;Deepdene Beach, your last long beach leg, offering a real sense of adventure and remoteness. Finish your journey at the historic&nbsp;Cape Leeuwin Lighthouse, where the Southern and Indian Oceans meet. Celebrate the end of your adventure before heading back to&nbsp;Waterwheel car park&nbsp;to collect your vehicle.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Packing List</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Clothing &amp; Footwear:</strong>&nbsp;Dress in layers to adapt to changing weather. Trail shoes or comfortable sneakers work best for the terrain.</p></li><li><p><strong>Essentials:</strong>&nbsp;Don’t forget sunscreen, insect repellent, blister care, and a head torch.</p></li><li><p><strong>Tech &amp; Hydration:</strong>&nbsp;Bring a power bank, swimwear, and water for Day 1.</p></li><li><p><strong>Seasonal Item:</strong>&nbsp;Fly net (recommended from November to December).</p><p><br></p></li></ul><p><strong>Safety First</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Navigation Apps:</strong>&nbsp;Download AllTrails (Pro version) or the Cape to Cape Navigation App for offline maps and easy route guidance.</p></li><li><p><strong>Emergency App:</strong>&nbsp;Install the St John First Responder App for quick access in emergencies.</p></li><li><p><strong>Track Conditions:</strong>&nbsp;The trail is well-marked, but navigation support offers extra peace of mind.</p><p><br></p></li></ul><p><strong>Food &amp; Drinks</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Meals:</strong>&nbsp;All meals are included, crafted with fresh, local ingredients by Inspired Feast.</p></li><li><p><strong>Dietary Options:</strong>&nbsp;Vegetarian and gluten-free options available upon request.</p></li><li><p><strong>Beverages:</strong>&nbsp;Enjoy water, coconut water, juice, tea, coffee, and a selection of local wine and beer.</p></li><li><p><strong>Snacks:</strong>&nbsp;Trail mix is provided, but feel free to bring extra snacks. We’ll transfer them with your hand luggage.</p><p><br></p></li></ul><p><strong>Comfortable Campsites</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Accommodation:</strong>&nbsp;Sleep in cosy twin-share tents, complete with inflatable mattresses, quilts, and pillows.</p></li><li><p><strong>Camp Setup:</strong>&nbsp;Walk-in, walk-out campsites ensure full immersion in nature—no daily transfers needed.</p></li><li><p><strong>Campfire Season:</strong>&nbsp;Campfires are allowed from 1 May to 1 November to enhance your outdoor experience.</p><p><br></p></li></ul><p><strong>Trail Ready</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Leave No Trace:</strong>&nbsp;Help protect nature by following Leave No Trace principles.</p></li><li><p><strong>Emergency Preparation:</strong>&nbsp;Download your navigation and emergency apps before your hike.</p></li><li><p><strong>Power Bank:</strong>&nbsp;Keep your devices charged with a portable power bank—especially useful on longer hikes.</p><p><br></p></li></ul><p><strong>Customisable Options</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Single Occupancy:</strong>&nbsp;Prefer a solo tent? Single occupancy tents are available as an add-on when booking.</p></li><li><p><strong>Equipment Rentals:</strong>&nbsp;Need hiking poles or a backpack? Rentals are available for your convenience.</p></li><li><p><strong>Gourmet Add-On:</strong>&nbsp;A snack pack will be waiting for you at camp—your little reward after a day of hiking.</p><p><br></p></li></ul><p><strong>Additional Information</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Vehicle Parking:</strong>&nbsp;Park your car where your hike ends; we’ll transfer you to the trailhead to get started.</p></li><li><p><strong>Private Groups:</strong>&nbsp;For 2 or more hikers, we offer flexible itineraries. Set your dates and we’ll design an experience tailored to your needs.</p></li><li><p><strong>Exclusions:</strong>&nbsp;Breakfast on Day 1 and accommodation before or after your Cape2Camp experience are not included.</p><p><br></p></li></ul><p><strong>Ready to Hike?</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Booking:</strong>&nbsp;A 20% deposit secures your spot. The remaining balance is due 10 days prior to your Cape2Camp adventure.</p></li><li><p><strong>Travel Insurance:</strong>&nbsp;We recommend travel insurance for peace of mind during your adventure.</p></li><li><p><strong>We Keep You on Track:</strong>&nbsp;For the full experience, day and night, we handle the logistics so you can focus on the adventure!</p></li></ul><h3><br></h3><p></p><p></p><p></p><p></p><p></p><p></p><p></p><p></p>",
